# Statistics

Summary statistics over real-valued sequences, pure LOGOS, identical on every tier. Auto-imported
on reference.

## Note
Arithmetic mean: sum of `xs` divided by its length.

## To meanReal (xs: Seq of Real) -> Real:
    Let mutable total be 0.0.
    Repeat for v in xs:
        Set total to total + v.
    Return total / (length of xs * 1.0).

## Note
Population variance: mean of squared deviations from the mean, dividing by `length of xs`.

## To pvarianceReal (xs: Seq of Real) -> Real:
    Let m be meanReal(xs).
    Let mutable acc be 0.0.
    Repeat for v in xs:
        Let d be v - m.
        Set acc to acc + d * d.
    Return acc / (length of xs * 1.0).

## Note
Population standard deviation: the square root of `pvarianceReal(xs)`.

## To pstdevReal (xs: Seq of Real) -> Real:
    Return sqrt(pvarianceReal(xs)).

## Note
Sample variance: sum of squared deviations from the mean divided by `length of xs - 1` (Bessel's correction).

## To varianceReal (xs: Seq of Real) -> Real:
    Let m be meanReal(xs).
    Let mutable acc be 0.0.
    Repeat for v in xs:
        Let d be v - m.
        Set acc to acc + d * d.
    Return acc / ((length of xs - 1) * 1.0).

## Note
Sample standard deviation: the square root of `varianceReal(xs)`.

## To stdevReal (xs: Seq of Real) -> Real:
    Return sqrt(varianceReal(xs)).

## Note
Harmonic mean: the count divided by the sum of the reciprocals of `xs`.

## To harmonicMeanReal (xs: Seq of Real) -> Real:
    Let mutable acc be 0.0.
    Repeat for v in xs:
        Set acc to acc + (1.0 / v).
    Return (length of xs * 1.0) / acc.

## Note
Returns `xs` sorted in ascending order using an O(n log n) stable mergesort.

## To sortReal (xs: Seq of Real) -> Seq of Real:
    Let n be length of xs.
    If n is at most 1:
        Return xs.
    Let mid be n / 2.
    Return mergeReal(sortReal(sliceReal(xs, 1, mid)), sortReal(sliceReal(xs, mid + 1, n))).

## Note
The `[lo, hi]` (1-indexed, inclusive) slice of a `Real` sequence.

## To sliceReal (xs: Seq of Real) and (lo: Int) and (hi: Int) -> Seq of Real:
    Let out be a new Seq of Real.
    Let mutable i be lo.
    While i is at most hi:
        Push item i of xs to out.
        Set i to i + 1.
    Return out.

## Note
Merge two already-sorted `Real` sequences, stable on equal elements.

## To mergeReal (a: Seq of Real) and (b: Seq of Real) -> Seq of Real:
    Let mutable out be a new Seq of Real.
    Let la be length of a.
    Let lb be length of b.
    Let mutable i be 1.
    Let mutable j be 1.
    Let mutable more be true.
    While more is equal to true:
        If i is greater than la:
            Set more to false.
        Otherwise:
            If j is greater than lb:
                Set more to false.
            Otherwise:
                If item i of a is at most item j of b:
                    Push item i of a to out.
                    Set i to i + 1.
                Otherwise:
                    Push item j of b to out.
                    Set j to j + 1.
    While i is at most la:
        Push item i of a to out.
        Set i to i + 1.
    While j is at most lb:
        Push item j of b to out.
        Set j to j + 1.
    Return out.

## Note
Median of `xs`: the middle element when the count is odd, else the average of the two middle elements.

## To medianReal (xs: Seq of Real) -> Real:
    Let s be sortReal(xs).
    Let n be length of s.
    If (n mod 2) is equal to 1:
        Return item ((n + 1) / 2) of s.
    Let lo be item (n / 2) of s.
    Let hi be item (n / 2 + 1) of s.
    Return (lo + hi) / 2.0.

## Note
Dot product: the sum of pairwise products `xs[i] * ys[i]` over the length of `xs`.

## To sumProdReal (xs: Seq of Real) and (ys: Seq of Real) -> Real:
    Let mutable total be 0.0.
    Let n be length of xs.
    Let mutable i be 1.
    While i is at most n:
        Set total to total + (item i of xs) * (item i of ys).
        Set i to i + 1.
    Return total.

## Note
Sum of all elements of `xs`, accumulated left to right.

## To fsumReal (xs: Seq of Real) -> Real:
    Let mutable s be 0.0.
    Let mutable c be 0.0.
    Repeat for v in xs:
        Let t be s + v.
        If absReal(s) is at least absReal(v):
            Set c to c + ((s - t) + v).
        Otherwise:
            Set c to c + ((v - t) + s).
        Set s to t.
    Return s + c.

## Note
Geometric mean: the product of `xs` raised to the power `1 / count`.

## To geometricMeanReal (xs: Seq of Real) -> Real:
    Let mutable s be 0.0.
    Let mutable cnt be 0.0.
    Repeat for v in xs:
        Set s to s + ln(v).
        Set cnt to cnt + 1.0.
    Return exp(s / cnt).

## Note
Sample covariance of `xs` and `ys`: the sum of products of paired deviations divided by `count - 1`.

## To covarianceReal (xs: Seq of Real) and (ys: Seq of Real) -> Real:
    Let mx be meanReal(xs).
    Let my be meanReal(ys).
    Let mutable s be 0.0.
    Let mutable cnt be 0.0.
    Let n be length of xs.
    Let mutable i be 1.
    While i is at most n:
        Set s to s + ((item i of xs) - mx) * ((item i of ys) - my).
        Set cnt to cnt + 1.0.
        Set i to i + 1.
    Return s / (cnt - 1.0).

## Note
Pearson correlation: the covariance of `xs` and `ys` divided by the product of their sample standard deviations.

## To correlationReal (xs: Seq of Real) and (ys: Seq of Real) -> Real:
    Let cov be covarianceReal(xs, ys).
    Let sx be stdevReal(xs).
    Let sy be stdevReal(ys).
    Return cov / (sx * sy).

## Note
Arithmetic mean of an integer sequence, returned as a Real via float division of the sum by the count.

## To meanInt (xs: Seq of Int) -> Real:
    Let mutable total be 0.
    Let mutable cnt be 0.
    Repeat for v in xs:
        Set total to total + v.
        Set cnt to cnt + 1.
    Return (total + 0.0) / (cnt + 0.0).

## Note
Least-squares regression slope: `covarianceReal(xs, ys)` divided by `varianceReal(xs)`.

## To linRegSlope (xs: Seq of Real) and (ys: Seq of Real) -> Real:
    Return covarianceReal(xs, ys) / varianceReal(xs).

## Note
Least-squares regression intercept: `meanReal(ys)` minus the slope times `meanReal(xs)`.

## To linRegIntercept (xs: Seq of Real) and (ys: Seq of Real) -> Real:
    Let slope be covarianceReal(xs, ys) / varianceReal(xs).
    Return meanReal(ys) - slope * meanReal(xs).

## Note
The `i`-th of `n` quantiles of `xs`, linearly interpolating between the two nearest sorted samples.

## To quantile (xs: Seq of Real) and (i: Int) and (n: Int) -> Real:
    Let s be sortReal(xs).
    Let ld be length of s.
    Let m be ld + 1.
    Let mutable j be (i * m) / n.
    Let delta be (i * m) mod n.
    If j is less than 1:
        Set j to 1.
    If j is greater than (ld - 1):
        Set j to ld - 1.
    Let lo be item j of s.
    Let hi be item (j + 1) of s.
    Return (lo * ((n - delta) + 0.0) + hi * (delta + 0.0)) / (n + 0.0).
